# Scratch drafts. Superseded by docs/design/. The copies here are older forks
# of the same files (tokens.md, the onboarding spec), so tracking them would put
# two versions of one document in the repo and leave the stale one to be found
# first. The maintained copies are the ones code cites.
scratch-drafts/

# Generated service keypairs. Never commit key material.
keys/

# Not part of the published source. deployment-guide.html is a second copy of
# docs/deployment.md that goes stale the moment the markdown is edited, and the
# Vault Ledger PDF is a 1 MB binary that cannot be diffed or reviewed. Both stay
# available to the team; neither belongs in a repository people read.
docs/deployment-guide.html
requirement/The Vault Ledger.pdf

# Round-1 audit analysis, kept out of the repo deliberately: it is an internal
# working record of every weakness found in this system, adjudicated per
# finding, and it is shared on request rather than shipped with the source.
# The remediation it produced is in the commit history; the analysis is not.
docs/audit-analysis/
docs/audit-analysis.zip

# Session handover notes. Working material, never published.
HANDOVER.md

# Dated internal design reviews: a screenshot-by-screenshot consistency pass, a
# UX run-through and a post-port feature audit. Working notes tied to a moment
# in the build, not documentation of how the system works.
docs/design/ux-review.md
docs/design/ui-consistency-pass.md
docs/design/feature-audit.md

# Specification, interface and operations documents. Kept with the team and
